// Classic's level editor for the machine that keeps the originals: all 175
// places of the original game in order, each beside its original. A place
// is a level in the game, or waits for a winnable layout and starts from the
// original board. Paint with the mouse, play with the keyboard, and let the
// solver check while you edit. Every change is kept as a draft at once, and a
// board saves itself into the game's levels as soon as a winning route the
// engine replays exists: the solver's, or yours from play mode. A waiting
// place then goes into the game in its place. Run from the Shovey root:
//
//     make editor && build/private-editor/shovey-level-editor
//
// Originals come from the ignored backup/original folder (classic-levels.zi
// and sprites/) and backup/redesign/stuck.txt; nothing original is built in.
//
// Edit: left button paints, right button clears to floor, Alt+click (or
// Shift+click) picks up the piece under the pointer, Z undoes a stroke,
// N / P change place, U goes to the next waiting place, [ / ] change the
// original shown, C checks now,
// Ctrl+S saves, Tab plays. Play: arrows or WASD, Space throws, Z undoes,
// R restarts, Tab goes back to editing.
